       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled dose of ibuprofen (3,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even with normal kidney function.\n\nHere are some typical regimens for an adult:\n- **Mild to moderate pain:** 400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed.\n- **Anti-inflammatory or arthritis dosing:** 400\u2013800 mg PO three to four times daily. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and it's usually best to use the lowest effective dose.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day)\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- Something else, such as 1,600 mg total per day\n\nIf you do want 1,600 mg per dose, tell me the clinical reason and I'll add that to the order note. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first."
